# Site-level locations the building references but never declared (2026-08-27).
#
# `bldg:BuildingExterior` is where feeds.yaml puts the three Open-Meteo weather
# points, and the feed framework registers them against it on every boot -- against
# a subject that appears in NO TTL. The same dangling-reference defect as the phantom
# AHUs (BUG-249), hidden from the TTL scan because the reference is made from a YAML
# file rather than from a triple.
#
# Found by diffing the live graph against what input/ can reproduce, before a rebuild.

@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix brick: <https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .
@prefix bldg:  <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#> .

bldg:BuildingExterior a brick:Outside ;
    rdfs:label "Building exterior" ;
    rdfs:comment "Outdoor location for weather observations taken at the building. Declared so the outside-air points that feeds.yaml registers here hang off a real subject." ;
    brick:isPartOf bldg:AbacwsBuilding .
